</ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Darwin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><source>The origin of species by means of natural selection</source><year>1882</year><publisher-name> John Murray London</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name></person-group><source>Systematics and the fossil record</source><year>1994</year><publisher-name> Blackwell Oxford</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bell</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Origin of metazoan phyla: Cambrian explosion or proterozoic slow burn?</article-title><source>Trends Ecol Evol</source><year>1997</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>2</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0169-5347(96)30048-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wills</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Fortey</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The shape of life: how much is written in stone?</article-title><source>BioEssays</source><year>2000</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>1142</fpage><lpage>1152</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11084630</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/1521-1878(200012)22:12&#x0003c;1142::AID-BIES12&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Peterson</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Butterfield</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Origin of the Eumetazoa: testing ecological predictions of molecular clock